      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe this is less of a bug and more to do with the limitations of the capsule collider system used to determine if an avatar is colliding with another object for the player controller. \n\nYour point is still valid but probably fits more in feature requests for when they eventually redo the movement system like they have talked about in the past. So that they might consider full IK collision to directly have an effect on avatar height allowing the user to stand/push/pull/sit on objects as an example as the avatar collides rather than an arbitrary primitive shape encapsulating the avatar. Capsule would still be useful for selecting a user, but as users locally calculate their position it is definitely possible to improve the precision with more accurate collision bounds perhaps defined by the avatar creator or automatically applied to the tracked points.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
