      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Really annoying when you lean over a ledge to look down but the game sends you falling because it thinks you are not on the ledge anymore as soon as you stick your head out too far even if your feet are planted on the ground.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-12T12:47:02.065Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Title basically. In worlds with relatively low chairs/tables with colliders (ones that can be stood on), attempting to bend over the chair so that you feet are on the floor and your head is over the chair would make the avatar float upwards, matching real floor (and avatar feet) with chair height.\nIt would be nice if user's feet (or maybe hips, or whatever the lowest point happens to be of hands/hips/head, idk) were used instead of their head for determining avatar vertical position, so that standing in place and bending over objects worked as intended and not caused me to float upwards.",
